// fileio_parallel.rho — Phase 10 canonical example
//
// Parallel byte-sum reduction over a File's byte stream using
// `foldConcurrent(init, combine, workers)`.  Illustrates the FIP
// §Stream parallel-combinator pattern: `combine` is invoked up to
// `workers` times concurrently; because addition is commutative and
// associative, the accumulator converges to the same value
// regardless of scheduling.
//
// Sequence:
//   1. Open a bundled File in "r" mode.
//   2. `file!bytes()` → `[true, byteStream]`.
//   3. Define `plus(returnCh, @acc, @byte) = returnCh!(acc + byte)`.
//   4. `byteStream!foldConcurrent(0, *plus, 8)` — sum every byte
//      value using up to 8 concurrent combine workers.
//   5. On `[true, total]`, print total.  On `[false, ...]`, print
//      the error.
//
// Convergence: for any commutative-associative `combine`, the result
// is well-defined independently of scheduling.  Under replay, the
// lead node's scheduling is captured in the produce log so followers
// re-derive the same accumulator; across local dev runs, the
// scheduling may vary but the mathematical result is stable.
//
// Impl note: `foldConcurrent`'s workers share a single mutex-
// protected accumulator cell.  Each worker pulls values from the
// source in parallel (the source's own state-lock serializes the
// pulls) but combines are strictly sequential within the shared
// cell.  This preserves fold-left order under replay and lets the
// user's `combine` retain the asymmetric `(acc, val) → acc`
// signature that `fold` also accepts (init is the initial acc; val
// is the stream's value type).  For CPU-heavy per-value work that
// benefits from concurrent invocation, prefer `mapReduce` (whose
// mapFn phase runs concurrently by design).
//
// Companion regressions: casper/tests/genesis/contracts/
// fileio_examples_spec.rs ::
//   fileio_parallel_byte_sum_sequential_variant     (via fold)
//   fileio_parallel_byte_sum_foldconcurrent          (this example)
//   fileio_parallel_byte_sum_of_squares_via_mapreduce (via mapReduce)

new
  rl(`rho:registry:lookup`),
  stdout(`rho:io:stdout`),
  fsCh,
  plus
in {
  rl!(`rho:id:zphjgsfy13h1k85isc8rtwtgt3t9zzt5pjd5ihykfmyapfc4wt3x5h`, *fsCh) |
  for(@(_, fs) <- fsCh) {
    for(@[true, file] <- @fs!?("openFile", "target", {"mode": "r"})) {
      for(@bytesReply <- @file!?("bytes")) {
        match bytesReply {
          [true, byteStream] => {
            contract plus(returnCh, @acc, @byte) = {
              // byteStream emits 1-byte ByteArrays (spec §Byte-stream
              // producer, File.rho line 1237); use `.nth(0)` to extract
              // the integer byte value.
              returnCh!(acc + byte.nth(0))
            } |
            for(@r <- @byteStream!?("foldConcurrent", 0, *plus, 8)) {
              match r {
                [true, total] => stdout!(("total byte sum", total))
                _             => stdout!(("foldConcurrent failed", r))
              }
            }
          }
          _ => stdout!(("file.bytes() failed", bytesReply))
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
